        {
          "id": 8,
          "title": "Signal Coverage",
          "type": "text",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 6,
            "w": 24,
            "h": 6
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "## Verified native Build 42 signals\n\n- **Live:** server FPS (not client rendering FPS), connected players, loaded/simulated/total zombies, animal instances and objects, loaded cells, daily events, process/JVM memory and CPU, sampled network rates, and online-player coordinates.\n- **Unavailable:** separate tick-rate metric; player health and inventory are deliberately excluded.\n- **No player online:** coordinate and roster series are absent, **not zero**. The roster is unavailable; the map can still show earlier positions within the selected time range.\n- **Semantics:** native `game`, `connection`, `performance`, and `network` series use a `parameter` label. Event charts show approximate rolling-hour increases from native game-day counters, which reset each game day. Process metrics are JVM-specific, never host totals. See [System Resources](/grafana/d/system-resources/system-resources) for host context.\n- **Signals:** retained Mimir metrics and Loki journal logs share `service=project-zomboid`, `host=habiki`. No alerts are provisioned."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
